research_rationale:
Identity: the held Federal Register text (27 FR 5699) prints Executive Order 11029 as an order of the President (John F. Kennedy) dated 1962-06-13; the number, subject and date agree with the census register row (subject: Amendment of Executive Order No. 
	11025, creating a Board of Inquiry to report on a labor dispute affecting the aircraft industry of the United States). I read the whole clause and signature block. Inventory: the dossier's single whole-order clause covers every operative sentence; I confirm it as complete. The one operative clause amends the title of Executive Order No. 11025 of June 7, 1962 and substitutes new text for its first and second paragraphs: recitals naming the parties to the dispute at the Republic Aviation Corporation facility and finding that the strike affects the tactical fighter production industry. It contains no command of its own beyond that rewriting and no date or condition of its own. Ending: EO 12553 of February 25, 1986, titled "Revocation of Various Executive Orders", orders that the listed Executive Orders, and "any amendments thereto, are revoked:" Its table lists this order by number and subject on one line: "11029 Amending an order creating a board of inquiry to report on a labor dispute affecting the aircraft". EO 12553 contains no effective-date wording (the held text was searched for effective, take effect, shall become, except, notwithstanding, nothing in, provided that and saving, with no hit outside table subjects); it is headed as an order of February 25, 1986 and signed that day, so the date is read as 1986-02-25, the signing date. The alternative reading is the Federal Register publication date, 1986-03-03 (Monday, March 3, 1986, 51 FR 7237); no later date is supported by the text. The quoted source for the end is the enacting paragraph of EO 12553, which names no order; the order is named by its row in the No./Subject table, quoted above, so the table row and the enacting paragraph are read together. Because the order only rewrites the text of EO 11025, it has no performance date, report deadline or sunset of its own; the amendment was effective when made and the rewritten text then formed part of EO 11025. EO 11025 is also listed in EO 12553 (its row reads "11025 Creating a board of inquiry to report on a labor dispute affecting the aircraft industry"). I read the complete held Federal Register copy of this order (27 FR 5699). No later held order names EO 11029 other than EO 12553; the catalog notes name EO 12553 as its revoking order. The earlier order EO 11026 also rewrote the first paragraph of EO 11025 and is itself listed in EO 12553; its relation to this order is described in the claim on EO 11026 and is not an event for this order. Savings: EO 12553 has no savings clause or exception. Searches selected after reading their coverage notes (all three complete, no coverage warning): U.S. Code release point 119-121 (no hit for this order), eCFR as of 2026-10-14 (no hit), and the Federal Register catalog disposition notes (2 machine hits, the revocation note on this order and the matching note on EO 12553).
Member checks: {"earlier_end_check":"No held source shows an earlier revocation, supersession, expiry or termination of this order. The own text has no end. I read the complete held Federal Register copy of this order (27 FR 5699). No later held order names EO 11029 other than EO 12553; the catalog notes name EO 12553 as its revoking order. The earlier order EO 11026 also rewrote the first paragraph of EO 11025 and is itself listed in EO 12553; its relation to this order is described in the claim on EO 11026 and is not an event for this order. The first ending shown by held evidence is the express revocation by number in EO 12553, effective 1986-02-25. Whether the Board of Inquiry created by EO 11025 ended earlier is a question for the claim on EO 11025 and does not supply an end for this separate amending order.","independent_command_check":"The order has no command independent of the text it amends; it creates no board, duty, deadline or authority of its own. No other order incorporating it was found in the held texts.","savings_check":"EO 12553 has no savings clause or exception (searched as described). Any effect the recitals had on the parent order's text was part of EO 11025 and is addressed in the claim on that order; no residual right or duty arises from this order.","scope_check":"Single clause, whole order: the amendment instruction and the quoted replacement recitals. I confirm the dossier inventory as complete. EO 12553 revokes the order by its own row, and also reaches amendments of the listed orders, so no part is left outside the ending."}
